{
	"type": "root",
	"children": [
		{
			"type": "yaml",
			"value": "title: Optimizing package bundling\nnav_title: Package Bundling\ndescription: Learn how to analyze and optimize your application's server and client bundles with the Next.js Bundle Analyzer for Turbopack, and the `@next/bundle-analyzer` plugin for Webpack."
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Bundling is the process of combining your application code and its dependencies into optimized output files for the client and server. Smaller bundles load faster, reduce JavaScript execution time, improve "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "https://web.dev/articles/vitals",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "Core Web Vitals"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": ", and lower server cold start times."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Next.js automatically optimizes bundles by code splitting, tree-shaking, and other techniques. However, there are some cases where you may need to optimize your bundles manually."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "There are two tools for analyzing your application's bundles:"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "list",
			"ordered": false,
			"start": null,
			"spread": false,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "listItem",
					"spread": false,
					"checked": null,
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "link",
									"title": null,
									"url": "#nextjs-bundle-analyzer",
									"children": [
										{
											"type": "text",
											"value": "Next.js Bundle Analyzer for Turbopack"
										}
									]
								}
							]
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "listItem",
					"spread": false,
					"checked": null,
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "link",
									"title": null,
									"url": "#nextbundle-analyzer-for-webpack",
									"children": [
