		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 3,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Give your AI agent access to the bundle analyzer"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "The "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "https://www.skills.sh/vercel/next.js/next-bundle-optimizer",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "inlineCode",
							"value": "next-bundle-optimizer"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " skill gives your AI agent access to the data powering Turbopack's bundle analyzer to automatically identify sources of large client-side bundles that impact your site's initial load performance."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "First, install the skill:"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "code",
			"lang": "bash",
			"meta": "filename=\"Terminal\"",
			"value": "npx skills add vercel/next.js --skill next-bundle-optimizer"
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Then prompt your agent. In audit-only mode, it produces a report without making any changes:"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "code",
			"lang": "prompt",
			"meta": null,
			"value": "Use the next-bundle-optimizer skill to produce a report of the initial load performance of this site."
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "You can also tell your agent to fix any issues, and it will optimize your site based on its findings. Or have it focus on a specific route by providing the route in the prompt."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 2,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "@next/bundle-analyzer"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " for Webpack"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "The "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "https://www.npmjs.com/package/@next/bundle-analyzer",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "inlineCode",
							"value": "@next/bundle-analyzer"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " is a plugin that helps you manage the size of your application bundles. It generates a visual report of the size of each package and their dependencies. You can use the information to remove large dependencies, split, or "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "./lazy-loading.md",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "lazy-load"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " your code."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 3,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Step 1: Installation"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Install the plugin by running the following command:"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "code",
			"lang": "bash",
			"meta": "package=\"pnpm\"",
			"value": "pnpm add @next/bundle-analyzer"
		},
		{
			"type": "code",
			"lang": "bash",
			"meta": "package=\"npm\"",
			"value": "npm install @next/bundle-analyzer"
		},
		{
			"type": "code",
			"lang": "bash",
			"meta": "package=\"yarn\"",
			"value": "yarn add @next/bundle-analyzer"
		},
		{
			"type": "code",
			"lang": "bash",
			"meta": "package=\"bun\"",
			"value": "bun add @next/bundle-analyzer"
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Then, add the bundle analyzer's settings to your "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "next.config.js"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "code",
			"lang": "js",
			"meta": "filename=\"next.config.js\"",
			"value": "/** @type {import('next').NextConfig} */\nconst nextConfig = {}\n\nconst withBundleAnalyzer = require('@next/bundle-analyzer')({\n\tenabled: process.env.ANALYZE === 'true',\n})\n\nmodule.exports = withBundleAnalyzer(nextConfig)"
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 3,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Step 2: Generating a report"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Run the following command to analyze your bundles:"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "code",
			"lang": "bash",
			"meta": null,
			"value": "ANALYZE=true npm run build\n# or\nANALYZE=true yarn build\n# or\nANALYZE=true pnpm build"
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "The report will open three new tabs in your browser, which you can inspect."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 2,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Optimizing large bundles"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Once you've identified a large module, the solution will depend on your use case. Below are common causes and how to fix them:"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 3,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Packages with many exports"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "If you're using a package that exports hundreds of modules (such as icon and utility libraries), you can optimize how those imports are resolved using the "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "../03-api-reference/05-config/01-next-config-js/optimizePackageImports.md",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "inlineCode",
							"value": "optimizePackageImports"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " option in your "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "next.config.js"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " file. This option will only load the modules you "
				},
				{
					"type": "emphasis",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "actually"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " use, while still giving you the convenience of writing import statements with many named exports."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "code",
			"lang": "js",
			"meta": "filename=\"next.config.js\"",
			"value": "/** @type {import('next').NextConfig} */\nconst nextConfig = {\n\texperimental: {\n\t\toptimizePackageImports: ['icon-library'],\n\t},\n}\n\nmodule.exports = nextConfig"
		},
		{
			"type": "blockquote",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "paragraph",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "strong",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": "Good to know:"
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": " Next.js also optimizes some libraries automatically, thus they do not need to be included in the "
						},
						{
							"type": "inlineCode",
							"value": "optimizePackageImports"
						},
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": " list. See the "
						},
						{
							"type": "link",
							"title": null,
							"url": "../03-api-reference/05-config/01-next-config-js/optimizePackageImports.md",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": "full list"
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": " of supported packages."
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 3,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Heavy client workloads"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "A common cause of large client bundles is doing expensive rendering work in Client Components. This often happens with libraries that exist only to transform data into UI, such as syntax highlighting, chart rendering, or markdown parsing."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "If that work does not require browser APIs or user interaction, it can be run in a Server Component."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "In this example, a prism based highlighter runs in a Client Component. Even though the final output is just a "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "<code>"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " block, the entire highlighting library is bundled into the client JavaScript bundle:"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "code",
			"lang": "tsx",
			"meta": "filename=\"app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx\"",
			"value": "'use client'\n\nimport Highlight from 'prism-react-renderer'\nimport theme from 'prism-react-renderer/themes/github'\n\nexport default function Page() {\n\tconst code = `export function hello() {\n    console.log(\"hi\")\n  }`\n\n\treturn (\n\t\t<article>\n\t\t\t<h1>Blog Post Title</h1>\n\n\t\t\t{/* The prism package and its tokenization logic are shipped to the client */}\n\t\t\t<Highlight\n\t\t\t\tcode={code}\n\t\t\t\tlanguage=\"tsx\"\n\t\t\t\ttheme={theme}>\n\t\t\t\t{({ className, style, tokens, getLineProps, getTokenProps }) => (\n\t\t\t\t\t<pre\n\t\t\t\t\t\tclassName={className}\n\t\t\t\t\t\tstyle={style}>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<code>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{tokens.map((line, i) => (\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tkey={i}\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{...getLineProps({ line })}>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{line.map((token, key) => (\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tkey={key}\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{...getTokenProps({ token })}\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t/>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t))}\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t))}\n\t\t\t\t\t\t</code>\n\t\t\t\t\t</pre>\n\t\t\t\t)}\n\t\t\t</Highlight>\n\t\t</article>\n\t)\n}"
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "This increases bundle size because the client must download and execute the highlighting library, even though the result is static HTML."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Instead, move the highlighting logic to a Server Component and render the final HTML on the server. The client will only receive the rendered markup."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "code",
			"lang": "tsx",
			"meta": "filename=\"app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx\"",
			"value": "import { codeToHtml } from 'shiki'\n\nexport default async function Page() {\n\tconst code = `export function hello() {\n    console.log(\"hi\")\n  }`\n\n\t// The Shiki package runs on the server and is never bundled for the client.\n\tconst highlightedHtml = await codeToHtml(code, {\n\t\tlang: 'tsx',\n\t\ttheme: 'github-dark',\n\t})\n\n\treturn (\n\t\t<article>\n\t\t\t<h1>Blog Post Title</h1>\n\n\t\t\t{/* Client receives plain markup */}\n\t\t\t<pre>\n\t\t\t\t<code dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: highlightedHtml }} />\n\t\t\t</pre>\n\t\t</article>\n\t)\n}"
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 3,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Opting specific packages out of bundling"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Packages imported inside Server Components and Route Handlers are automatically bundled by Next.js."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "You can opt specific packages out of bundling using the "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "../03-api-reference/05-config/01-next-config-js/serverExternalPackages.md",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "inlineCode",
							"value": "serverExternalPackages"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " option in your "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "next.config.js"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "code",
			"lang": "js",
			"meta": "filename=\"next.config.js\"",
			"value": "/** @type {import('next').NextConfig} */\nconst nextConfig = {\n\tserverExternalPackages: ['package-name'],\n}\n\nmodule.exports = nextConfig"
		},
		{
